    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Now consider a univariate random variable $ y = \\sum c_k x_k $ generated from a linear combination of the elements of x. In matrix notation, $ y = c^T x $, where c is a column vector of constants. The variance of y can be expressed as a quadratic form involving the covariance matrix V for the elements of x,",
